            "review_title": "Review at Mr. BBQ & SsAm",
            "review_text": "Traveler of the Wild\nHo Chi Minh City, Vietnam66 contributions\n0\nVietnamese Korean BBQ- Not bad but not excellent\nFeb 2018 • Couples\nThis is a Viet-Korean restaurant with pretty good food and a nice clean environment. Is it authentic Korean? Definitely not. Although the meats were of a good quality there was a decidedly lacklustre line-up of Korean side dished (no Geranjim (steamed eggs), no dwenjang jigae (soy bean paste soup) offered, The side dishes were far below the standard expected in District 7 (Saigon's Korea town). However, the service was friendly and efficient. One slight downer was that they wouldn't allow Dwaeji-galbi or Sam Gyeap Sal (both pork BBQ dishes) to be cooked at the table. This is an annoying local thing that would never happen in Korea. Drinks.........they had Soju and basic industrial beers but at the price range and clientele in the local area (the posh side of district 7) you need to be offering a wide range of Korean wines, craft beers and so on. Overall, a decent experience but overpriced for the quality. Also, someone perhaps should advise that in Korean and most western cultures, it's not appropriate to touch a 5 month old baby without permission from the parents.\nRead more\nValue\nService\nFood\nWritten February 4, 2018",
            "rating": 5.0,
            "review_date": "2026-10-14",
            "travel_date": "Recent",
            "feature_depth_status": "Schema-Full-Features-Validated"
        },
