            "review_text": "maryyeo\nHo Chi Minh City, Vietnam4531 contributions\n0\nGood portions, Good prices, I like it!\nMar 2015 • Couples\nWas there a few times - see the owner quite often and he'll always be talking to his staff for improvements, etc. He's on top of things. \n\nThe Korean food offered there feels more like Korean street food, which is fun to eat especially if you don't want to be too full (e.g. after doing the spa just next door owned by the same owner). Having said that, they are generous with their portions. My favourite dish is their cheese toppokki... it is usually double the price somewhere else in Phu My Hung but theirs was about 100k and yet has lots of seafood and cheese. Their panchan which comes complimentary is also delicious. Their hu tiu nam vang also has lots of ingredients. Overall, their food is rather cheap and yet better than some other places we've tried in the area!\nRead more\nReview collected in partnership with this restaurant \nWritten February 18, 2016",
